description: 'Trigger ONLY when the user provides the result set of an already-executed
  Cortex XSIAM search and asks to summarize, explain, or narrate what the logs show
  for SOC triage. Accepts the results as a rendered table (column headers such as
  _time and event_type plus rows), JSON row objects, or CSV. The skill condenses the
  rows, reconstructs the chronological event story, highlights notable users, hosts,
  IPs, and processes, and suggests next investigative steps in plain language. The
  output is always a written Markdown briefing. Examples: "summarize these logs",
  "explain what these events show", "narrate this XSIAM result set". Do not activate
  for writing or running searches, authoring detection rules, extracting IOCs, assigning
  verdicts, recommending remediation, or non-XSIAM/raw packet formats.'
